# scripts/opcount: `readerbench bench mapreplay N` reads a Map of four
# keys N times from a codec.Replay of its events, on the prelude's Reader
# interface (JSON-CURSOR-ALLOC): each key the Map keeps is a copy
# (stdlib.md json 2), though a Replay's keys are its own. The control is
# hand Go: encoding/json into a map[string]int.
unit read
sizes 20000 120000
args bench mapreplay {n}
control benchmarks/wirereaders/testdata/control
